WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.810
Speaker 1: All right, let's get into audience
questions for the week, a bunch of questions

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.679
about the recent 60 Minutes UFO UAP piece
that was done.

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:15.079
The general gist of the question is, is David,
what's your view about the truth of the recent

00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:16.160
UFO UAP story?

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:23.800
Now, UAP is a relatively, at least in the
public space, new term for unidentified foreign

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.730
objects called unidentified aerial phenomena,
I'm sorry, unidentified flying objects.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:35.030
The new UAP is unidentified aerial phenomena.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:43.420
My view on this is I don't think anybody is
lying about what they believe they saw.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.850
When you see pilots interviewed and saying
we saw this moving in that way at the speed

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:48.879
and we don't know this, that.

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:53.750
The other thing I believe everybody so far
is being honest in their perceptions.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.429
I believe we only have part of the story and
I have no evidence at this point that we are

00:00:58.429 --> 00:01:00.840
dealing with aliens from another planet.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:04.790
And this is the most important thing to remember
just because we say there's a UFO that's an

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.360
unidentified flying object.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:11.140
It's an object that's flying and we don't
know exactly what it is, doesn't mean that

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:12.140
it's aliens.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.970
And similarly, an unidentified aerial phenomena
has the sort of same analysis.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:28.840
Now, I've said before, if there is an intelligent
interstellar traveling species or human society

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:33.079
of some kind that comes to the United States.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:38.950
If we default to treating it as a threat,
the way, for example, Marco Rubio said these

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.130
UAP UFOs are, these are threats.

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:48.680
Well, it may be a threat if they are you know,
if it's spy technology from an adversary,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.330
then we're talking about national security.

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:56.520
But if we did get a visit from aliens and
we treat it as a threat when they are actually

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:03.650
not a threat, if they come in peace, so to
speak, then we could potentially destroy what

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:09.210
would be a historic species changing encounter.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:14.360
And the reality is that at this point, since
we lack the technology to do what we imagine,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:19.450
maybe someday would happen, which is some
huge alien race from somewhere else in the

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.140
universe comes to the United States.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:26.760
If they came with nefarious goals, it's abundantly
clear that at least at this time, we would

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.640
be able to do nothing to prevent them from
either killing all of us or enslaving all

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:31.640
of us or whatever.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:38.140
So for me, the national security analysis
makes more sense if we're conceding that the

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:43.830
most likely explanation is that this is either
something from a foreign power.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:50.350
In which case, by the way, if we really don't
understand what it is, then they are way further

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.450
ahead than us in many ways.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.290
And we should be extremely worried.

00:02:55.290 --> 00:03:03.340
Or it's also possible that these are unidentified
or unknown to the pilots and people that were

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:08.760
interviewed for the 60 Minutes piece, but
that it actually is classified at a level

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.720
above their pay grade or level of access.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.480
And the people who know what these things
are did not participate because maybe 60 Minutes

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.120
doesn't even know who they are.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:27.310
So I think my main point here is that for
me, the most serious approach to this UFO

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:34.790
UAP thing is, first of all, there is no evidence
that this is aliens from somewhere other than

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:35.790
Earth.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:36.790
There's just no evidence of that.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:42.180
And it's fascinating to think of and I understand
the equations about the probability of intelligent

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.100
life other than just on Earth Earth.

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.970
And I recognize that if we were ever to make
that first contact, that would truly be an

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.970
incredible thing.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.230
I'm not saying it's not possible.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.700
I'm just saying there's no evidence that this
is that.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:59.790
Then it gets to the question of assuming that
it is indeed manmade technology, then what

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.790
is the source of it?

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.990
Is it something American that is so classified
that even the people interviewed don't know

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:06.630
what it is?

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:07.870
Or is it something foreign?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:11.370
And then you get the people who say, well,
the physics of it doesn't make sense.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:19.350
There were dissents in altitude that would
have killed any human body that was in there.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.290
OK, maybe there wasn't a human body in there.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:27.450
We also know that the way a lot of these things
are filmed and perspective and lenses can

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:32.040
make something seem different than what it
might look like to the naked eye.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:38.940
The where I come back to is sort of an Occam's
razor type question, which is which of these

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:41.930
explanations require the fewest assumptions?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:46.840
And the ones that require the fewest assumptions
are the visual perception that the pilots

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.120
claim is not entirely accurate.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.470
That would be a very straightforward way to
explain away a lot of this or this is stuff

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.470
that is known.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.710
It's not unidentified.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.760
It was unidentified to the pilots and maybe
to air traffic control.

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:08.880
But it's technology that higher up we are
aware of or it was human made technology from

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.530
some other like from some other country.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:16.030
The one that is the furthest and requires
the most assumptions, of course, would be

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:22.480
the alien one, which is there is an alien
species that is advanced enough to travel

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.270
to Earth from really far in the universe because
we've been observing the universe that's more

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:34.440
immediately around us for a very long time
and to do it without any other signature radiowaves

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.230
or whatever else.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.840
And so the number of assumptions start to
go up significantly.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.390
So that's not where I am on this.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.010
Now, just one other thought on this.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.740
One thing I read was.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:49.810
The information that was released.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:56.440
Was fake information released by the U.S.
government to trick other countries?

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:57.440
What's the idea here?

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.430
This is quite cynical and.

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.580
If you go down this rabbit hole, the pilots
interviewed on 60 Minutes could be in on it

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.330
or not, they might not even be in it.

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:12.920
The idea would be let's make some video and
have pilots tell stories or otherwise convince

00:06:12.920 --> 00:06:17.710
pilots of the reality of this so that 60 Minutes
will do a piece, will have some big reveal

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.330
about these UAP UFOs.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:27.480
And this will be seen by our adversaries and
it will completely misdirect them so that

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:32.840
they will start sinking R&amp;D money into what
they think they need to do to develop these

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:33.840
things.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:36.610
And it's just it's either digital, it's not
even real.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:43.310
It's just been made on a computer and it's
a way to get adversaries to spend.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.860
Unfortunately, that's not totally implausible
compared to the alien theory.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:54.960
The deliberate misdirection campaign by by
the U.S. government strikes me as more plausible.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:55.960
Send me your thoughts.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:54.730
That's kind of where my head is on this at
this point 

00:07:54.730 --> 00:08:03.740
in time.

